{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Wooden door creaks open",
  "description": "A heavy old panelled door pushed slowly open on dry iron hinges, in a stone-floored hallway. The hinge pin sticks and slips: a train of tiny clicks so fast it becomes a groan. It unsticks with a quick stutter, settles to a rough purr of about 40 slips a second, climbs to a whining 175 as the door speeds up through the middle of its swing, falters, then drops back to separate ticks as the door comes to rest after 1.8 s. The door panel is the loudspeaker for the hinge: it gives the groan its woody, vowel-like colour.",
  "tags": [
    "door",
    "creak",
    "open",
    "wood",
    "hinge",
    "squeak",
    "haunted",
    "horror",
    "slow"
  ],
